# The session log is append-only by ritual (AGENTS.md): every task adds its
# entry at the end and never edits another's. Two branches that both append to
# the end of the same file conflict every single time, because Git sees two
# different lines claiming the same position with no shared context between
# them. That is structural, not bad luck, and no amount of process documentation
# prevents it.
#
# `union` is Git's built-in driver for exactly this shape: on a conflict it
# keeps both sides in full instead of stopping. That is precisely what every
# session has been doing by hand, so this automates the existing convention
# rather than changing it.
#
# It is safe here only because the ritual forbids rewriting or deleting another
# session's entry. Do not extend `union` to files where two branches can edit
# the same region, such as pubspec.yaml or any structured config, where keeping
# both sides would produce a file that no longer parses.
docs/SESSION_LEARNINGS.md merge=union
